\
  Use this order:\
\
  Context:\
  - Repository:\
  - Branch:\
  - Source repository:\
  - Active database:\
  - Current worktree state:\
\
  Objective:\
  - Exact outcome required.\
\
  Source of truth:\
  - Files, tables, functions, or commands that must be inspected.\
\
  Scope:\
  - Files allowed to change.\
  - Files explicitly out of scope.\
  - Whether database/graph refresh is allowed.\
\
  Execution order:\
  1. Investigation\
  2. Plan\
  3. Implementation\
  4. Review\
  5. QA\
  6. Smoke test\
\
  Agent contracts:\
  - Planner: read-only, return root cause, touch points, risks, tests.\
  - Implementer: edit only approved files, add regression tests.\
  - Reviewer: read-only, attempt to falsify the fix.\
  - QA: independently run commands and report exact results.\
\
  Safety:\
  - Preserve unrelated worktree changes.\
  - Do not delete active/previous databases.\
  - Stop and ask if state or ownership is ambiguous.\
\
  Acceptance criteria:\
  - Exact tests and expected outcomes.\
  - Required lint/compile checks.\
  - Required database/provenance checks.\
  - Known residual risks.\
